  "answer": "Only 2 of the 5 cases were confirmed, so the goal was not met. The confirmed cases are scene 02eadd92 at the recorded speed and timing (S1) and scene 054b5901 at 1.2x speed with the recorded timing (S4); every run at both failed. Neither case comes from retiming the crossing car. Both are at 0 s shift, S1 fails at the default settings, and on 054b5901 the ego left the road or ran into the back of a different car (car 9), not crossing track 93. In every failure the policy ignored a RIGHT command and drifted left, more than 3.5 m off its recorded path, so every failure is also flagged as a possible simulator artifact. Shifting the crossing car's timing never caused a collision with it on any scene, so the study found no speed-and-timing combination that makes VaVAM with the linear MPC fail against the crossing car.",
